        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: prevent connection retention on guarded redirect failures",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where guarded HTTP redirects could leave an unread response body attached to the dispatcher when the redirect was rejected because of a missing or invalid `Location`, a loop, or the redirect limit. Repeated failures could delay connection reuse and retain transport resources.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nCancel and await every redirect response body before validating the next hop, while preserving the existing redirect, authorization, and dispatcher cleanup behavior. Cancellation failures remain non-fatal.\n\n## User Impact\n\nGuarded fetch callers now cleanly release redirect responses on all rejection paths, improving reliability under repeated malformed or looping redirects without changing accepted redirect behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before the fix, four focused regression cases observed zero body cancellations.\n- [Real local-server + Undici shard](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29594148985/job/87930500031): 102 focused fetch-guard tests passed; 3 real Undici tests passed in 291 ms. Each uses an ephemeral loopback server with a body left open, requires rejection within 1 second, and verifies server-observed sockets return to zero for missing-location, loop, and redirect-limit failures.\n- [Original failing web-fetch shard](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29594148985/job/87930500035): 11 tests passed in 191 ms, including the private-host redirect case that previously failed.\n- [Lint/format](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29594148985/job/87930499604): oxlint passed and oxfmt reported all files correctly formatted.\n- [Full CI gate](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29594148985/job/87931705365): passed on head `d4fb379b6c10ab7dcae4bba4cc7a6f3fa3b75284`.\n- `git diff --check` passed; final whole-branch autoreview was clean with no accepted/actionable findings (0.96).\n- Undici documents that response bodies must be consumed or canceled for connection reuse: https://github.com/nodejs/undici#garbage-collection\n- Privacy: proof ran in secretless fork CI against an ephemeral loopback server. No credentials, private endpoints, IPs beyond loopback, or agent transcript were included.\n- AI-assisted; I reviewed the diff and understand the behavior.\n",
